<title>FRANCE: TAT-Liberte airlines stay on strike.</title>
<headline>TAT-Liberte airlines stay on strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Striking cockpit crews at British Airways units TAT and Air Liberte forced the two French-based companies to cancel about 60 percent of their combined schedule on Tuesday, the companies said.</p>
<p>Unions, protesting over pay and conditions which they say will be affected by a merger of the two airlines, urged management to negotiate.</p>
<p>Marc Rochet, chairman of the two units, has rejected demands for reforms which he said would raise wage costs by 18 percent.</p>
</text>
